<section class="content-section" id="what-section">
    <div class="content-container">
        <div class="two-column">
            <div class="column-content">
                <h2 class="section-title">What Is LLP Name Change?</h2>
                <div class="content-text what-is-definition">
                    
                    <p>LLP name change is the formal legal process of altering the registered name under Section 19 of the LLP Act, 2008. The name appears on the Certificate of Incorporation, LLPIN, all MCA records, PAN, GST, bank accounts, contracts, and every legal document. Changing it requires MCA approval through a structured process.</p>
                    <p>Two routes exist: (1) Voluntary change under Section 19 &ndash; business reasons (rebranding, expansion, partnership change), requiring partner consent and ROC approval via Form 5. (2) Directed change under Section 20 &ndash; ROC/Central Government orders change because name is identical/similar to existing entity or trademark. For <a href="/trademark-registration">Trademark Registration</a> to protect your new name, see our page.</p>
                    <p>The name change has practical business implications: client-facing materials, contracts (addendums needed), bank accounts, and GST invoices must all reflect the new name from the change date. For <a href="/legal-drafting">Legal Drafting</a> of supplementary deeds, see our page. Patron manages the complete transition for Mumbai LLPs.</p>

                </div>
                <div class="highlight-box" style="margin-top:20px;">
                    <p><strong>Key Terms for LLP Name Change:</strong></p>
                    <ul>
                        <li><strong>Section 19:</strong> Voluntary LLP name change with partner consent and ROC approval</li>
                        <li><strong>Section 20:</strong> Directed change &ndash; ROC/Central Government orders if name is undesirable or too similar</li>
                        <li><strong>RUN-LLP:</strong> Reserve Unique Name &ndash; up to 2 names, Rs 200, valid 20 days</li>
                        <li><strong>Form 5:</strong> Notice for Change of Name &ndash; approval-based filing with ROC</li>
                        <li><strong>Form 3:</strong> Supplementary LLP Agreement &ndash; linked form within 30 days of Form 5</li>
                        <li><strong>Fresh COI:</strong> New Certificate of Incorporation issued by ROC with new name and same LLPIN</li>
                    </ul>

                </div>
